%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 225d9ba1d6472414ca12190972df08df, type: 3}
  m_Name: tutorial_05
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  loadState: 0
  questId: 
  tutorialId: 
  tutorialSlides:
  - tutorialTitle: Potion Brewing
    tutorialVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 1c013c3d6c44a634fa5fbb168191522b, type: 3}
    tutorialDescription: Ready to make some potions? this will be where all the potion
      brewing happens. first of all, open the recipe list on the bottom left of the
      screen and choose a recipe to brew.
  - tutorialTitle: Potion Brewing
    tutorialVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 4771a5bd2b281fd4ca552e0ea0804771, type: 3}
    tutorialDescription: To successfully brew a potion, you must get the water surface
      to match the shape of the guideline of the selected potion recipe.
  - tutorialTitle: Potion Brewing
    tutorialVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 8720fa6f043492a48a6454c6bee1cb3f, type: 3}
    tutorialDescription: You can adjust the height of the water surface by pulling
      the chains on the side up or down.
  - tutorialTitle: Potion Brewing
    tutorialVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 3b793574d5569844bb87c8fc44e9b10d, type: 3}
    tutorialDescription: By hovering your cursor on a herb, it will show how they
      will effect the water surface when added into the cauldron. Potions requires
      more the one herb to brew.
  - tutorialTitle: Potion Brewing
    tutorialVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 490d64adf507df642969ea3e9b6971d6, type: 3}
    tutorialDescription: By holding left click on the herbs you can drag and move
      it around. Releasing the left click will drop the herbs, dropping it anywhere
      outside the cauldron will return it to your inventory.
  - tutorialTitle: Potion Brewing
    tutorialVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 03539e0eb11bb4542a65d57a5a0b3845, type: 3}
    tutorialDescription: Dropping the herbs into the cauldron will change the water
      surface, where you drop the herbs effect the shape as well so keep it in mind.
  - tutorialTitle: Potion Brewing
    tutorialVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: db5d7b48823337f40834699be1d5dc20, type: 3}
    tutorialDescription: Each potion recipe have their main herb, these herb will
      always be drop in the middle of the cauldron. You can learn which herb is the
      main ingredient of which potion in your journal.
  - tutorialTitle: Potion Brewing
    tutorialVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: ef910d742b550374eb5db5492f06bf99, type: 3}
    tutorialDescription: 'If you ever made a mistake, click the Redo button on the
      middle left of the screen. This will refund the herb used back into your inventory. '
  - tutorialTitle: Potion Brewing
    tutorialVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 7c6aff99aae73e1408efcdc20d813948, type: 3}
    tutorialDescription: The undo button on the bottom left will restart the brewing
      process and refund all of the herbs used back into the inventory.
  - tutorialTitle: Potion Brewing
    tutorialVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 669b90bc2b9547f4b815c3a418a15d7b, type: 3}
    tutorialDescription: 'Once your water surface match with the recipe guideline,
      press the brew button to finally brew your potion. TIp: all potions require
      a minimum of 2 herbs.'
  - tutorialTitle: Potion Brewing
    tutorialVideo: {fileID: 32900000, guid: b9dfe6b2e17189546adc23485c392c72, type: 3}
    tutorialDescription: If you ever get confuse you can press the Question Mark
      label in the journal to re-read this tutorial. Good luck brewing alchemist
      !
